~ matt_ch2_start
Matt: The sea has its own rules. When the tide rises and falls, we must follow them.
Player: Why should we follow the rules of the sea?
Matt: The sea gives us food. We must respect and take good care of it, so that it can nourish us forever. Humans and nature must get along well.
do QuestState.mark_chapter2_quest1_matt_done()
=> END

~ kai_ch2_start
Kai: I want to use new methods: ecological breeding, regular fishing moratorium, and low-carbon fishing.
Player: Can traditional experience and innovation work together?
Kai: Yes. Let the small fish grow up before catching; then there will always be fish in the sea.
do QuestState.mark_chapter2_quest1_kai_done()
=> END

~ jessica_ch2_start
Jessica: Look, there is a lot of garbage on the beach, and the seawater is not as clean as before.
Player: Are the fish getting fewer too?
Jessica: Yes! The fish we catch now are getting smaller and fewer. If we don’t take good care of the sea, there will be no fish in the future.
do QuestState.mark_chapter2_quest1_jessica_done()
=> END

~ aurora_ch2_residents_start
Aurora: I can help sort shells and bottles too. Let’s keep the beach clean together every day.
=> END

~ villagers_ch2_warehouse_start
Matt: We elders never catch too much, leaving time for the sea to recover. This is respect for nature.
Kai: I want to use new methods, ecological breeding, regular fishing moratorium, let the small fish grow up before catching. In this way, there will always be fish in the sea.
Player: You are both for the good of the sea! Traditional experience and new methods can be used together! Learning from each other can make things better.
do QuestState.mark_chapter2_quest3_warehouse_done()
=> END

~ matt_ch2_quest3_start
Matt: We elders never catch too much, leaving time for the sea to recover. This is respect for nature.
=> END

~ kai_ch2_quest3_start
Kai: I want to use new methods, ecological breeding, regular fishing moratorium, let the small fish grow up before catching. In this way, there will always be fish in the sea.
